  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q16-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "16",
    "prompt": "The hypotenuse of a right-angled triangle has length $8+\\sqrt{3}$. Another side has length $4\\sqrt{3}+2$.\n\nFind:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p14-q16-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "the length of the third side",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt{15}$",
          "worked": "Let the third side have length $x$. By Pythagoras’ theorem,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+(4\\sqrt{3}+2)^2&=(8+\\sqrt{3})^2\\\\x^2&=(8+\\sqrt{3})^2-(4\\sqrt{3}+2)^2\\\\x^2&=(64+16\\sqrt{3}+3)-(48+16\\sqrt{3}+4)\\\\x^2&=15\\\\x&=\\sqrt{15}\\end{align*}$$\n\nTake the positive square root because $x$ is a length.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q16-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "the perimeter of the triangle",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$10+5\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{15}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P&=(8+\\sqrt{3})+(4\\sqrt{3}+2)+\\sqrt{15}\\\\P&=10+5\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{15}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q16-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "the area of the triangle",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$6\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{15}$\n\nUse the two perpendicular sides as the base and height.",
          "worked": "The perpendicular sides have lengths $4\\sqrt{3}+2$ and $\\sqrt{15}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac{1}{2}(4\\sqrt{3}+2)\\sqrt{15}\\\\A&=2\\sqrt{45}+\\sqrt{15}\\\\A&=6\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{15}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      }
    ]
  },
